# Quality gates

Vitest and GitHub Actions CI already exist (see `docs/roadmap.md` Priority
P2). Design code to be testable (pure use cases, injectable ports) and follow:

## Testing

- **Unit tests**: application use cases (`apps/api/src/application/**`), pure
  functions, and mappers — Vitest, no real database. Prefer small in-memory
  fakes implementing repository ports (project convention; no mocking
  framework required).
- **Integration tests**: Prisma repositories against a real test database —
  still deferred; do not invent a full test-DB harness unless that is the
  scoped task.
- **E2E smoke tests**: critical user flows (login, create application, add
  round → question → skill evaluation) — Playwright still deferred unless
  scoped.
- New use case ⇒ add/update its unit test in the same change when practical.
- Do not test framework internals (Hono routing, Prisma itself).

## CI/CD

- CI runs on push/PR to `main`: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm format:check`,
  `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build` (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`).
- Migrations run as a release step (`prisma migrate deploy`), never inside
  request handlers or app startup code.
- Each environment (dev/staging/prod) gets its own `DATABASE_URL` and secrets
  via platform env config, not via separate code branches.
- Lockfile (`pnpm-lock.yaml`) stays committed; CI installs with
  `--frozen-lockfile`.
